"""Passage register for J. Jayalalithaa; retrieval gaps are retained."""
ASOF='2026-10-26'
sources,retrievals=[],[]
def src(n,title,author,url,date,kind,locator,passage,note='',status='Passage inspected',origin=None):
    sid=f'S{n:03d}'
    sources.append({'Source ID':sid,'Title':title,'Author / institution':author,'Publication date':date,'URL':url,'Access date':ASOF,'Source class':kind,'Primary / secondary':'Primary' if kind in ('Official record','Court record','Legislation','Primary statement','Survey analysis') else 'Secondary','Access status':status,'Origin ID':origin or sid,'Locator':locator,'Reliability / limitation':note or 'Evidence applies to the specified period and passage; it does not establish exclusive personal causation.'})
    retrievals.append({'id':f'R{n:03d}','source_id':sid,'url_or_query':url,'access_date':ASOF,'route':'Canonical source or identified reproduction','access_status':status,'origin_id':origin or sid,'locator':locator,'passage_paraphrase':passage,'method':'web.run passage inspection','result':'Relevant passage inspected' if status=='Passage inspected' else note,'next_action':'Revisit only with a better route or new evidence.'})

src(1,'Cabinet condoles the demise of Selvi J Jayalalithaa','Government of India, PIB','https://www.pib.gov.in/newsite/PrintRelease.aspx?lang=2&reg=48&relid=155076','2016-12-07','Official record','Resolution paragraphs 1–4','Born 24 February 1948 at Mysore; schooling in Bengaluru and Chennai; film career; AIADMK entry 1982, Rajya Sabha election 1984, Assembly election and first woman opposition leader in 1989. Died 5 December 2016.','Commemorative resolution. Broad Mysore birthplace retained; exact locality not resolved. Its five continuous CM spells combine the two 2015–16 ministries.')
src(2,'Chief Ministers of Tamil Nadu since 1920','Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly','https://www.assembly.tn.gov.in/history/cmlist.php',None,'Official record','Jayalalithaa entries, retrieved lines 60–69','CM entries: 24 June 1991–12 May 1996; 14 May–21 September 2001; 2 March 2002–12 May 2006; 16 May 2011–27 September 2014; 23 May 2015–21 May 2016; 23 May–5 December 2016. Janaki held office in January 1988.','The list ends the fifth ministry on 21 May 2016; other summaries use 22 May or continuous service. Preserve source convention without inferring a one-day vacancy. Some unrelated entries also overlap.')
src(3,'Obituary reference: J. Jayalalithaa','Rajya Sabha, Synopsis of Debate','https://cms.rajyasabha.nic.in/UploadedFiles/Synopsis/SynopsisUpload/241/06122016.pdf','2016-12-06','Official record','Printed p.57','Represented Tamil Nadu in Rajya Sabha April 1984–January 1989; twice opposition leader; film work in Tamil, Telugu and Kannada.','Synopsis explicitly is not an authoritative verbatim record. Exact Rajya Sabha resignation day is not settled here; the five-CM-spell phrasing is not a count of oath-taking ceremonies.')
src(4,'J Jayalalithaa: The Amma and the daughter','Arun Janardhanan, Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/india/jayalalithaa-dead-heart-attack-amma-tamil-nadu-4412542/','2016-12-06','Journalism','Career paragraphs, lines 41–58','Schooling preceded cinema. MGR mentorship and propaganda work led to campaigning during his illness. Succession was contested with Janaki’s faction. Describes Sasikala’s influence, Brahmin background and a tightly controlled party.','Retrospective reporting contains loose dates for imprisonment and tenure. Those details are not adopted; personal details used only for political pathways.')
src(5,'Amma','Indian Express editorial board','https://indianexpress.com/article/opinion/editorials/j-jayalalithaa-death-funeral-rajaji-hall-cardiac-arrest-tamil-nadu-4414141/','2016-12-07','Opinion','Editorial paragraphs, lines 50–60','Editorial credits resilience within patriarchal cinema and politics, welfare delivery and broader support; also criticises autocratic leadership, personality cult and weak second-rung development.','Attributed editorial interpretation, not a causal impact evaluation or neutral measurement of leadership.')
src(6,'B.R. Kapoor v. State of Tamil Nadu','Supreme Court; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/499867/','2001-09-21','Court record','Final majority order, lines 437–447; opening account','Court quashed the 14 May 2001 CM appointment because statutory disqualification prevented appointment under Article 164. Otherwise valid governmental acts were protected through the de facto doctrine.','Separate from later acquittal in the underlying criminal cases; reproduces judicial text rather than a signed official scan.')
src(7,'R. Sai Bharathi v. J. Jayalalitha','Supreme Court; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/447378/','2003-11-24','Court record','Concluding discussion and disposition, lines 316–328','Appeals against acquittal in TANSI transactions dismissed. Court nevertheless criticised conflict of interest and conduct inconsistent with public probity, and called for unconditional return of property.','Acquittal is the criminal disposition; adverse ethical observations are not a conviction. Do not conflate this matter with disproportionate assets.')
src(8,'State of Karnataka v. Selvi J. Jayalalitha and others','Supreme Court; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/135095591/','2017-02-14','Court record','Opening and concluding disposition, lines 115, 2786–2801','Challenges the 11 May 2015 acquittal. Appeals against deceased Jayalalithaa abated. The court examined her role and restored trial-court conviction and sentence for surviving accused A2–A4.','Not a new posthumous conviction of Jayalalithaa. Abatement does not erase the judgment’s adverse factual discussion or amount to merits exoneration.')
src(9,'T.K. Rangarajan v. Government of Tamil Nadu','Supreme Court; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/1501031/','2003-08-06','Court record','Right-to-strike reasoning; reinstatement arrangements, lines 135–183','Court held government employees had no fundamental right to strike. It recorded mass dismissals, extensive reinstatement and arrangements for retired High Court judges to consider remaining representations.','Do not describe the decision as approval of every dismissal. Reinstatement conditions and categories differed.')
src(10,'Flood management and response in Chennai and its suburban areas, Report 4 of 2017','Comptroller and Auditor General of India','https://www.cag.gov.in/uploads/download_audit_report/2017/Report_No_4_of_2017_-_Performance_Audit_of_Flood_Management_and_Response_in_Chennai_and_its_Suburban_Area.pdf','2017','Official record','Executive summary p.x and paragraph 5.8.5','Audit criticises drainage, delayed desilting, reservoir forecasting and release management during the 2015 floods.','Initial search extraction inspected; full document inspection pending. This is an audit finding concerning agencies, not a criminal finding against the CM.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(11,'Daughter Elimination: Cradle Baby Scheme in Tamil Nadu','Sharada Srinivasan and Arjun S. Bedi, EPW 45(23), 17–20; UNFPA mirror','https://www.unfpa.org/sites/default/files/resource-pdf/UNFPA_Publication-39835.pdf','2010-06-05','Scholarship','Printed pp.17,19–20; scheme, contribution and Looking Ahead sections','Salem scheme began in 1992; surrender intended as an alternative to infanticide. Authors estimate a possible contribution to reduced post-birth daughter deficit, while most improvement came from other measures; poor follow-up data and civil-society criticism remain.','Study covers multiple administrations. An illustrative accounting estimate is not experimental causal identification; survival, placement and underlying son preference are distinct.',origin='SRINIVASAN-BEDI-2010')
src(12,'CM inaugurates 127 Amma Unavagams','New Indian Express','https://www.newindianexpress.com/cities/chennai/2013/apr/03/cm-inaugurates-127-amma-unavagams-464389.html','2013-04-03','Journalism','Lines 51–57','First 15 centres opened 19 February 2013. April inauguration brought one centre to each of Chennai’s 200 wards. Women’s self-help groups operated them; idli Rs1, sambar rice Rs5 and curd rice Rs3.','Contemporary implementation report; benefit assertions are not an independent nutrition or poverty evaluation.')
src(13,'List of Amma Unavagam','Greater Chennai Corporation','https://chennaicorporation.gov.in/gcc/citizen-details/location-service/ser_ammaunavagam.jsp',None,'Official record','Location table','Municipal register lists canteen locations by zone, division and street.','Current administrative listing supports institutional continuation, not the number operating in 2013 or service quality in 2026.')
src(14,'Tamil Nadu’s water revolution','Sam Daniel, NDTV','https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/tamil-nadus-water-revolution-402085','2009-09-24','Journalism','Report narrative','Reports 2003 ordinance requiring harvesting structures in old and new buildings and Jayalalithaa’s compulsory-policy role.','Uses enthusiastic outcome language and anecdotes. Its claim that scarcity ended is not adopted; no controlled groundwater effect is established.')
src(15,'Roof Top Rain Water Harvesting','PIB, Government of India','https://www.pib.gov.in/newsite/PrintRelease.aspx?lang=2&reg=48&relid=101516','2013','Official record','State table, Tamil Nadu row 21','Existing and new buildings in Tamil Nadu must provide rainwater harvesting facilities under municipal laws.','Administrative description of requirement; neither compliance nor hydrological effectiveness measured.')
src(16,'Constitution (Seventy-sixth Amendment) Act, 1994','Parliament of India; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/171366294/','1994','Legislation','Objects and reasons paragraphs 4–9; section 2','State legislation maintained 69% reservation; Union amendment placed Tamil Nadu Act 45 of 1994 into Ninth Schedule. Records unanimous Assembly and all-party steps.','Existing quota was protected, not invented by Jayalalithaa. Ninth-Schedule placement must not be described as permanent immunity from all constitutional review.')
src(17,'Tamil Nadu Prohibition of Forcible Conversion of Religion Act, 2002','Tamil Nadu Gazette via India Code','https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/20496/1/the-tamil-nadu-prohibition-of-forcible-conversion-of-religion-act-2002.pdf','2002','Legislation','Section 3 and original enactment','Prohibits conversion by force, allurement or fraudulent means.','Original act located; section passage appears in search extraction. Complete enactment/repeal chain not yet inspected.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(18,'Jaya accepts defeat','Times of India','https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/jaya-accepts-defeat/articleshow/683576.cms','2004-05','Journalism','Government reversal statement','Reports withdrawal of anti-conversion policy, employee-strike proceedings and other measures after the 2004 parliamentary defeat. Quotes her claim that the original law sought religious harmony.','Complete statement available in search extraction; formal repeal instrument and 2006 legal dispute require separate checking.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(19,'Jaya meets President, withdraws support','Rediff, contemporary report','https://www.rediff.com/news/1999/apr/14jaya.htm','1999-04-14','Journalism','Lines 19–30','Jayalalithaa gave President Narayanan a letter withdrawing the 18-MP AIADMK’s support to Vajpayee’s coalition. She said the President would decide the next constitutional step.','Headline body mislabels BJP once; only the clearly identified event and her reported statement are used.')
src(20,'Fall of the Government by a Single Vote','Lok Sabha Secretariat, Journal of Parliamentary Information','https://eparlib.sansad.in/bitstream/123456789/763158/1/jpi_September_1999.pdf','1999-09','Official record','Article beginning printed p.145','Distinguishes withdrawal from coalition coordination on 9 April and formal letter on 14 April 1999.','Official PDF timed out in browser and direct retrieval; indexed passage only. Full division and parliamentary account remain a research lead.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(21,'State of Tamil Nadu v. State of Kerala','Supreme Court; Indian Kanoon reproduction','https://indiankanoon.org/doc/41744252/','2014-05-07','Court record','Mullaperiyar reasoning and concluding relief','Court rejected Kerala’s attempt to negate the previous judgment; allowed restoration to 142 feet with a three-member supervisory committee.','A state-government litigation result drawing on engineers, lawyers and long litigation; not exclusively a personal achievement or a current dam-safety assessment.')
src(22,'Why the jury is still out on March 25, 1989 assembly row','New Indian Express, archival reconstruction','https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/tamil-nadu/2023/aug/21/why-the-jury-is-still-out-on-march-25-1989-assembly-row-2607286.html','2023-08-21','Journalism','Lines 53–64','Violence occurred during the 1989 budget session. Jayalalithaa alleged Duraimurugan pulled and tore her sari; he and DMK denied it. Later witnesses differed over the acts and severity.','Includes contemporaneous newspaper material and later recollections. Supports existence of violence and conflicting accounts, not a conclusive adjudication of the specific disrobing allegation.')
src(23,'Tamil Nadu Assembly election results 1989','Elections.in, secondary election table','https://www.elections.in/tamil-nadu/assembly-constituencies/1989-election-results.html','1989 results','Election compilation','Bodinayakkanur row 133, line 155','Jayalalithaa 57,603; Muthu Manoharan, DMK, 28,872; winning party ADK(JL).','Fallback after original ECI retrieval failed. Gender column incorrectly marks her M and is rejected. Modern boundary and spelling variants must not overwrite historical seat.')
src(24,'Tamil Nadu Assembly election results 1991','Elections.in, secondary election table','https://www.elections.in/tamil-nadu/assembly-constituencies/1991-election-results.html','1991 results','Election compilation','Bargur row 78 and Kangayam row 117','Bargur: Jayalalithaa 67,680, T. Rajhendher (TMK) 30,465. Kangayam: Jayalalithaa 69,050, N.S. Rajkumar Mandradiar (DMK) 35,759.','Two constituency victories in one general election, not two Assembly terms. Primary originals remain open; percentages withheld.')
src(25,'Tamil Nadu Assembly election results 1996','Elections.in, secondary election table','https://www.elections.in/tamil-nadu/assembly-constituencies/1996-election-results.html','1996 results','Election compilation','Bargur row 78','E.G. Sugavanam, DMK, 59,148; Jayalalithaa 50,782.','Secondary fallback; candidate-minus-opponent margin is negative because she lost.')
src(26,'Victory margin of Jaya her all-time best','Rediff, election agency report','https://m.rediff.com/election/2002/feb/24_bye_agen_rep_11.htm','2002-02-24','Journalism','Lines 25–27','Andipatti victory: 78,437 candidate votes and 41,201 margin.','Opponent votes 37,236 are derived from reported votes and margin, not independently transcribed. Article total 134,703 conflicts with other summaries; share withheld.')
src(27,'Tamil Nadu Assembly election results 2006','Elections.in, secondary election table','https://www.elections.in/tamil-nadu/assembly-constituencies/2006-election-results.html','2006 results','Election compilation','Andipatti row 135, line 164','Jayalalithaa 73,927; Seeman, DMK, 48,741.','Secondary fallback; the opponent is identified as DMK’s Seeman, not assumed to be the later NTK leader.')
src(28,'Srirangam constituency result 2011','Pollmedia, transcription of ECI detailed table','https://pollmedia.org/india/constituency?code=139&edition=23cc38bf6d2d08576d05c3ff&kind=ac&name=Srirangam&state=Tamil+Nadu','2011 results','Election compilation','2011 candidate table','Jayalalithaa 105,328; N. Anand, DMK, 63,480.','Page labels publication review pending and has inconsistent summary figures. Use only candidate counts corroborated by other compilations; primary return still needed.')
src(29,'Jayalalithaa wins R K Nagar seat by 1.5 lakh margin','Press Trust of India via Financial Express','https://www.financialexpress.com/india-news/chennai-counting-for-rk-nagar-by-polls-begins-jayalalithaa-future-at-stake/91989/lite/','2015-06-30','Journalism','Final-round result paragraph','Jayalalithaa 160,432; C. Mahendran 9,710; total 181,420 including 2,376 NOTA, leaving 179,044 votes for candidates.','Same PTI origin in syndications; not multiple independent sources. Share denominator explicitly includes NOTA.',origin='PTI-RKNAGAR-2015')
src(30,'Jaya retains R K Nagar seat','Press Trust of India via Business Standard','https://www.business-standard.com/article/pti-stories/jaya-retains-r-k-nagar-seat-116051901238_1.html','2016-05-19','Journalism','Result paragraph','Jayalalithaa 97,218; Shimla Muthuchozhan, DMK, 57,673; margin 39,545.','Contemporary result; no denominator supplied, so a checked vote share is not inferred.',origin='PTI-RKNAGAR-2016')
src(31,'Tamil Nadu Assembly election and government formation','Lok Sabha Secretariat, Journal of Parliamentary Information','https://eparlib.sansad.in/bitstream/123456789/58525/1/JPI_September_2016.pdf','2016-09','Official record','Assembly Election Results, Tamil Nadu section','Polling on 16 May 2016; AIADMK 134, DMK 89, Congress 8, IUML 1; two seats deferred.','Indexed passage only so far; distinguishes 232 declared seats from 234 Assembly strength.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(32,'Jayalalitha Speaks, Volume 3','Jayalalithaa speeches; Tamil Digital Library','https://tamildigitallibrary.in/assets/docs/uploads/primary_files/book/TVA_BOK_0025740/TVA_BOK_0025740_Jayalalitha_Speaks_Volume_3.pdf',None,'Primary statement','Printed p.127','She described women-staffed stations and economic independence as policy aims; claimed a 1992 starting date.','Interested first-person account. Claims to being first in India or the world are not adopted; exact first-station month needs police records.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(33,'TN Assembly adopts Sri Lanka resolution','NDTV','https://www.ndtv.com/india-news/tamil-nadu-assembly-adopts-resolution-centre-must-stop-treating-sri-lanka-as-a-friendly-country-517407','2013-03-27','Journalism','Lines 280–284','Resolution moved by Jayalalithaa sought international investigation, economic embargo and a referendum on Eelam; arose amid student protests and competition with DMK.','State political demand, not implementation of sanctions or an independently adjudicated genocide finding.')
src(34,'Sasikala rejects Jayalalithaa death-inquiry report','Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/cities/chennai/jayalalithaa-death-probe-panel-report-sasikala-reaction-8217405/','2022-10-19','Journalism','Report and Sasikala statement','Arumughaswamy commission criticised Sasikala and others; she denied interfering with treatment and said she would face inquiry.','Commission recommendation is not a criminal conviction. Full report, exhibits and subsequent disposition have not been collected.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(35,'No errors found in treatment given to Jayalalithaa: AIIMS team','ETB Sivapriyan, Deccan Herald','https://www.deccanherald.com/india/no-errors-found-in-treatment-given-to-jayalalithaa-aiims-team-1137834.html','2022-08-20','Journalism','Indexed report of AIIMS panel; page headline','Reports AIIMS medical board found treatment consistent with correct medical practice.','Browser exposed headline and metadata but not complete body. Full panel report not inspected. Retained as a countervailing lead, not a medical conclusion.',status='Search excerpt only')
src(36,'Tamil Nadu Medical Services Corporation','Tamil Nadu Health and Family Welfare Department','https://www.tnhealth.org/tnmsc.htm',None,'Official record','Institutional history, lines 23–24','Incorporated 1 July 1994; procurement, storage and distribution began January 1995; objective to ensure essential drug availability in government institutions.','Establishment during her tenure does not by itself show sole personal design; bureaucratic and subsequent contributions matter.')
src(37,'Vision Tamil Nadu 2023, Volume I','Government of Tamil Nadu; TNAU mirror','https://agritech.tnau.ac.in/pdf/2012/TN%20Vision%202023_Volume%20I.pdf','2012','Official record','Foreword, introduction and target sections; PDF pp.6–11,35–38','Strategic infrastructure plan covering power, transport, industry, health and education; targets real GSDP growth around 11% and outlines sector plans and implementation stages.','Targets and planned projects are not realised growth or completed infrastructure. Tenure ended before the plan horizon.')
src(38,'Lokniti-CSDS post-poll analysis: Women bought Jaya her return ticket','Rahul Verma and P. Ramajayam, Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/india/india-news-india/jayalalithaa-aiadmk-dmk-tamil-nadu-assembly-elections-2016-results2815867/','2016-05-24','Survey analysis','Lines 40–50; discussion of Figures 4–6','Survey estimates AIADMK led DMK alliance by 10 percentage points among women; women more often rated Jayalalithaa favourably as administrator. Authors say reasons require deeper investigation.','Survey association, not an individual voting record or proof that gender alone caused victory. Cross-tabs do not isolate one welfare scheme.')
src(39,'Jayalalithaa sworn in as MLA from RK Nagar','Business Standard reporter','https://www.business-standard.com/article/politics/jayalalithaa-sworn-in-as-mla-from-rk-nagar-115070400213_1.html','2015-07-04','Journalism','Result and election context paragraphs','Reports 160,432 versus 9,710 votes and major-party boycott. Srirangam seat lost after trial conviction; Karnataka High Court acquittal preceded return as CM.','Different by-election competition makes simple 2015–16 share comparisons misleading.')
src(40,'2016 Tamil Nadu result: Opposition surge and welfare','Arun Janardhanan, Indian Express','https://indianexpress.com/article/elections-2016/india/india-news-india/tamil-nadu-assembly-elections-results-jayalalithaa-aiadmk-amma-welfare-schemes-2810036/','2016-05-20','Journalism','Election result and campaign interpretation','AIADMK won 134 of 232 seats contested in May; first consecutive state-election victory since MGR in 1984. Reporting connects welfare reach with retention.','Election result is factual; explanation of why people voted is interpretation, checked against survey S038.')

